# CODEOWNERS: who gets auto-requested for review on which paths.
#
# Right now you are solo, so everything routes to you. That looks pointless --
# it is not. It means the day someone else commits, the routing already exists
# and nobody has to remember to set it up. It also makes the "these areas are
# sensitive" judgement explicit and reviewable.

# Default owner for everything
*                       @kirtidhwajpatra

# Audio is the product. Nothing here changes without an owner's eyes on it.
/HUMMI/AudioEngine/     @kirtidhwajpatra
/HUMMITests/            @kirtidhwajpatra

# Release and CI machinery: a bad change here can ship a broken build to users
# or leak a credential.
/.github/               @kirtidhwajpatra
/fastlane/              @kirtidhwajpatra
/Gemfile                @kirtidhwajpatra
/Gemfile.lock           @kirtidhwajpatra

# Project file conflicts are subtle and easy to merge wrongly.
/HUMMI.xcodeproj/       @kirtidhwajpatra
